Q: How does an agentic retriever differ from a fixed pipeline, and how is it evaluated?
A: An agentic retriever “decides at each step whether it has enough information or should search again” [d4], while a fixed pipeline is a “fixed single-pass pipeline” [d6]. So the key difference is that the agentic retriever can iteratively choose to retrieve more information, rather than doing only one predetermined pass.

It is evaluated by “comparing its answers and cost against a fixed single-pass pipeline” [d6].
